%I A329495 #15 Nov 10 2026 21:44:46
%S A329495 1,4,25,101,655,11077,94199,2005319,62541113,530615357,3888615949,
%T A329495 2547768661,1603125774433,510235838011,76538488318091,
%U A329495 10462945272539099,182249306891497151,7488308007918913129,6810487755999748187
%N A329495 Numerator of second moment of the n-th term of Ulam's "history-dependent random sequence".
%C A329495 Ulam's sequence is X_{n+1} = X_n + X_{U(n)}, X_0 = 1, U(n) independent and uniform on {0, ..., n}. Then a(n)/A329496(n) = E[X_{n-1}^2]. - _Gage Bonner_, Nov 04 2026
%H A329495 Gage Bonner, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1017/jpr.2026.10136">On the moments of the Ulam-Kac adder</a>, J. Appl. Probab. (2026).
%H A329495 Mark Kac, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0196-8858(89)90014-6">A history-dependent random sequence defined by Ulam</a>, Advances in Applied Mathematics 10.3 (1989): 270-277. See page 273, sigma_k and alpha_k.
%F A329495 From _Gage Bonner_, Nov 04 2026: (Start)
%F A329495 Let s(n) = a(n+1)/A329496(n+1) = E[X_n^2]. The g.f. G(z) = Sum_{n>=0} s(n)*z^n satisfies (z^2 - 6*z + 7)*G(z) + (3*z - 8)*(1 - z)^2*G'(z) + (1 - z)^4*G''(z) = 0, G(0) = 1, G'(0) = 4 (Bonner 2026, Section 2).
%F A329495 With s(n) as above, (n+1)^2*s(n) - 2*(n+2)*(2*n+5)*s(n+1) + (n+3)*(6*n+19)*s(n+2) - 4*(n+3)*(n+4)*s(n+3) + (n+3)*(n+4)*s(n+4) = 0, with s(0..3) = 1, 4, 25/2, 101/3.
%F A329495 For every m >= 1, log(E[X_n^m]) ~ c_m*sqrt(n), where c_m = 2*sqrt(lambda_m) and lambda_m is the Perron-Frobenius eigenvalue of an explicit integer matrix (Bonner 2026, Theorem 1.1). For m = 2 this is due to Kac (1989), with c_2 = sqrt(2*(5+sqrt(17))). (End)
%e A329495 1, 4, 25/2, 101/3, 655/8, 11077/60, 94199/240, 2005319/2520, ...
%p A329495 s:=[1]; a:=[0];
%p A329495 for N from 2 to 40 do # N = n+1
%p A329495 n:=N-1;
%p A329495 t1:=s[n]+(1/n)*add(s[k],k=1..n)+2*s[n]/n+(2/n)*a[n];
%p A329495 t2:=s[n]+(1/n)*add(s[k],k=1..n)+a[n]+(2/n)*add(a[k],k=1..n);
%p A329495 s:=[op(s),t1];
%p A329495 a:=[op(a),t2];
%p A329495 od:
%p A329495 s; # sigma_n
%p A329495 a; # alpha_n
%p A329495 sn:=map(numer,s); # A329495
%p A329495 sd:=map(denom,s); # A329496
%p A329495 an:=map(numer,a); # A329497
%p A329495 ad:=map(denom,a); # A329498
%Y A329495 Cf. A329496, A329497, A329498.
%K A329495 nonn,frac,changed
%O A329495 1,2
%A A329495 _N. J. A. Sloane_, Nov 17 2019
